<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply cut in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply cut in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to February 10 by reducing the amount of repos outstanding and by reducing credits granted at the weekly tender.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   441.25 (+  2.97)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  13.15 (-  2.88)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.74 (-  0.28)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.84 (-  0.01)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	  88.42 (-  4.66)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   446.08 (+  1.75)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
